  "grammar": {
    "title": "Telling the time: half drie, kwart over vier",
    "points": [
      "Hoe laat is het? = What time is it? Answer: Het is drie uur. (uur stays singular.)",
      "om = at: om drie uur = at three o'clock. Hoe laat begint de les? Om acht uur.",
      "over = past, voor = to: tien over twee (2:10), vijf voor drie (2:55). kwart over vier = 4:15, kwart voor vijf = 4:45.",
      "Careful: half looks ahead to the next hour. half drie = 2:30 (halfway to three), not 3:30!",
      "Around the half hour, count from half: vijf voor half drie = 2:25, tien over half drie = 2:40.",
      "In everyday speech the Dutch use the 12-hour clock."
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "nl": "Het is drie uur.", "en": "It's three o'clock." },
      { "nl": "Het is half drie.", "en": "It's half past two. (2:30)" },
